        <tr>
            <td colspan=2>
                <p>Verify that the Intel Hitachi chamber stainless steel run card is included inside of the lid of the transit case. Inspect the run card to confirm that the Intel verification section has been signed off by outgoing Intel technicians.<br>Using ESCA/QA, print of a work order for the relevent kit to be refurbished. Also print of a copy of the work order label and place on the transit case the kit was received in. The completed kit must be shipped back in the same transit case.</p>

                <p>Check all parts for knicks, scratches, and bends to the edges and O-ring sealing surfaces. If any nonconformities are found regarding the run card or with the parts, contact the Production Manager.</p>

                <p>The procedure for any non conformities found is to use a "yellow tag" process. Once a non conformity is found, note details of this onto the hard copy of the work order, entering as much details as possible such as part name, damage type such a scratch or dent, location of the damage on the part etc. Also state that the part is to be labelled with a "yellow tag" at final inspection.</p>

                <p>A tracking sheet should be set up to document and capture all "yellow tag" non conformities found. All nonconformities need to be relayed to the tool/part owner for disposition. Once disposition is obtained, the tracking sheet should be populated with this information. This tracking sheet can then be referenced each time the kit/parts are sent of refurbishment and that the same parts does not need to be &quot;yellow tagged&quot; each time its received and inspected.<br>Check shipping case for damage inlcuding castors, latches, hinges or other damage. Report any damage found to Production Manager. All parts within a kit shall be processed as a batch and not mixed with another kit.</p>
